{
  "name": "tasks-categories",
  "description": "Tasks, categories and event deletion in two calendars: a storage calendar and an ics calendar seeded with two events and three tasks. listCategories returns the configured names sorted; createTask (direct, in a named calendar, in the default one) is visible in listTasks with its due date and priority; updateTask completes, reopens, sets a percentage, changes title, due date (date only, date-time, cleared), description and priority, and listTasks (completed, dueBefore, maxResults, table) reflects it, as does the .ics file written by Thunderbird; deleteEvent removes a seeded event from listEvents and from the file; an event created with categories lists them. The main errors are checked (unknown calendar or task or event, bad date, bad priority, missing argument, completed together with percentComplete, nothing to change). Limits: updateTask and deleteEvent work on seeded items; the review dialog of createTask is only opened here (calendar-review-outcome.json drives it). Nothing is sent.",
